# X : emit the push of a word's or an atom's runtime address.
#
# This is the body of the ′ case, lifted out into a word because M-CHAIN2's
# chain definitions need the same thing three times over: "push the address of
# the thing named by this byte".  A defined word has a body to point at.  An
# ATOM does not — it is a template in the blob, not callable code — so its
# template is wrapped in a thunk [prologue][template][epilogue], emitted inline
# and jumped over, and the thunk's address is pushed instead.  That is what
# makes ′+ and a chain link like ÷ work without the user wrapping anything.
# A name that is neither may be a word defined further down (M2 for long names,
# W10-A for one-byte ones): push a forward thunk, patched by its definition.  If
# it never comes (`′typo`) it is rejected exactly as a plain call to it would
# be — `GOLF: undefined word <name>`, exit 2, at end of input (W9-1C, W10-A).

