# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Locals (M-FRAME, sized per definition since M-FRAME2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A ⊡ word's locals are NAMES — `a`…`h` or any ‹long name› — and each gets the
# next slot at its first appearance in the definition, so a word that names k
# locals has a frame of exactly k cells: slot i at [rbp+8*i], the return address
# at [rbp+8*k].  The slot is known the moment the name is read, so ⇒/⇐ stay
# five fixed bytes; only k is not known until `;`, and that is the frame-size
# immediate's problem (see ⊡, `^` and `;` in `t`).  At most 16 locals, which
# keeps every displacement a disp8 (8*15 = 120 < 128).

